ERE lease_id=L1\n           -> zero rows, but old code logs and continues in one error path\nbrowser: receives seq 12 succeeded, then delayed seq 10 started\n```\n\nThe correct result is one terminal projection and one terminal event. A stale worker may be\nallowed to finish its expensive local render, but it must not mutate the job or publish a\nsuccess event after losing ownership. A failed conditional update is a normal domain result,\nnot a reason to emit an event using the stale `version` it read earlier.\n\nThe SSE route also has a boundary race: it queries rows through sequence 12, then subscribes\nto Redis, while a publisher sends sequence 13 between those operations. A robust route either\nsubscribes before taking a replay watermark and filters duplicates, or performs a second durable\nread after subscribing. The fix must retain tenant and job predicates on every read and should\nnot rely on a client-supplied `Last-Event-ID` job id to select authorization scope.\n\n## Task\n\n## Task\n\nDiagnose the incident and propose a minimal, production-quality refactor. Trace the relevant\ninterleavings through the API transaction, worker transaction, outbox publisher, SSE replay,\nand browser reducer. Identify every invariant that the current excerpts violate. Then provide\nan implementation-oriented answer with the smallest set of file changes needed to ensure that:\n\n1. concurrent identical `POST /v1/jobs` requests with one tenant and one idempotency key create\n   exactly one job and return the same response;\n2. a terminal job cannot be reopened by a delayed or duplicated event in either the durable\n   projection or the browser;\n3. event sequence allocation and the job projection remain atomic, including worker progress and\n   completion;\n4. a worker that loses its lease cannot publish a successful completion;\n5. SSE replay and live delivery do not produce a visible regression or a permanent gap.\n\nInclude concrete TypeScript/SQL patches or focused pseudocode for the critical methods, and add\ntests for the two races described above. Call out any behavior that should be handled as a\nseparate follow-up instead of being smuggled into the minimal fix. Keep the response focused on\nthis repository and task; do not invent a new messaging platform.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","has_new_line":true,"truncated":false,"stop_type":"limit","stopping_word":"","tokens_cached":8030,"timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":7903,"prompt_ms":127391.393,"prompt_per_token_ms":16.119371504491966,"prompt_per_second":62.03715819325408,"predicted_n":128,"predicted_ms":23543.787,"predicted_per_token_ms":185.38414960629922,"predicted_per_second":5.394204424292489}}}


